launch------This utility adds to the login environment established by tsmon and login. It is intended to allow a single login to be used from different models of terminal - something that is not possible with the standard shell, as the .login script cannot contain conditional statements. It is necessary to set the TERM environment string to match the terminal and to ensure that key bindings in .umacsrc suit the terminal.Launch sets up TERM and PATH environment strings from the /dd/sys/config file. TERM is set to the terminal type defined for the port. If a search path is defined in the file it replaces the value set by login. The file containstwo types of entry, each forming a separate line. Use any text editor to maintain them:Terminal type definitions:	port=termtypePath definition:			PATH=searchpath							EDITIN=macro_root							EDITOUT=macro_filee.g.,	/t1=pc		/t2=wyse120		/t3=vt100		PATH=/dd/local/cmds:/dd/sculptor/cmds:/dd/cmds		EDITIN=/dd/sys/umacsrc.		EDITOUT=.umacsrcTermtype names are validated against entries in /dd/sys/termcap and the 'is' capability, if it is defined, is output to initialise the terminal if the -i option is present; otherwise the 'rs' capability is used.If the -e option is present an editor initial bindings file is set up by copying a prototype. The source file is formed by appending the terminal name to the macro_root defined by the EDITIN entry in the configurationfile. It is copied to the filename defined by the EDITOUT entry in theconfiguration file. The output file is written to the home directory, overwriting any existing copy.Author	Martin Gregorie	10 Sadlers Mead	Harlow	Essex	CM18 6HG	Gregorie@LFGMS.logica.com